#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hidraw-interface.md:2
msgid "hidraw interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hidraw-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"`hidraw` enables raw access to USB and Bluetooth Human Interface (*hidraw*) "
"devices. This interface is restricted because it provides privileged access "
"to hardware devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hidraw-interface.md:6
msgid "**Auto-Connect**: no **Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hidraw-interface.md:8
msgid "Should specify a single path attribute:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hidraw-interface.md:9
msgid "`path` (slot): path to hidraw device node e.g. /dev/hidraw0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hidraw-interface.md:10
msgid "Or three attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hidraw-interface.md:11
msgid ""
"`usb-vendor` (slot): integer representing the USB Vendor ID, must be in "
"range 0 < vid <= 65535"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hidraw-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"`usb-product` (slot): integer representing the USB Product ID, must be in "
"range  0 <= vid <= 65535"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hidraw-interface.md:13
msgid ""
"`path` (slot): path where a symlink will be created to the device e.g. `/dev/"
"hidraw-mydevice`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hidraw-interface.md:15
msgid ""
"To use a hidraw device, the snap developer must add `plugs: [ hidraw ]` to a "
"snap's [snapcraft.yaml](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/"
"reference/project-file/anatomy-of-snapcraft-yaml/). The snap user can then "
"access a specific hidraw device with an {ref}`interface connection "
"<explanation-interfaces-all-about-interfaces>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hidraw-interface.md:17
msgid ""
"Use  `snap interface hidraw` to see which hidraw devices are available on "
"the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hidraw-interface.md:19
msgid ""
"Once connected, the consuming snap can use the device via the path specified "
"by the connected slot."
msgstr ""
